MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-11 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Apply comprehensive knowledge of industrial management, analytical principles, process flow, depot operations, material procurement and financial principals;
2) Demonstrate ingenuity when problems arise for which a solution is not covered by instructions/ directions or policies;
3) Adapt analytical techniques and evaluate criteria to the measurement and improvement of program effectiveness;
4) Effectively communicate orally and in writing. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-11 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Providing program management and advice to the organization concerning energy and water conservation programs;
2) Applying analytical evaluation methods and techniques to issues or studies concerning the efficiency and effectiveness of energy program operations;
3) Managing energy mandates, programs, and processes to develop energy and water conservation programs and to conduct related training to installation personnel; and
4) Researching legislation, studies, policies, and procedures to provide guidance on an organizational energy program. NOTE: This information must be fully supported in your resume. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

Details.Education:
For the GS-11 level only, education may be substituted for experience as follows: Successful completion of a Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree;
OR
Successful completion of three full years of progressively higher level graduate education leading to a Ph.D. or equivalent degree;
OR
Successful completion of an LL.M. degree that is related to the position being filled. https://www.usajobs.gov/Help/working-in-government/unique-hiring-paths/students/federal-occupations-by-college-major/;
OR
A combination of experience and graduate education as described above that equates to one year of experience. The percentage of required education plus the percentage of required experience must equal one hundred percent.

MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-07 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: (1) Provides administrative and evaluative work relating to inventory management, program cost, processes and procedures, evaluation of program efficiency and effectiveness, and management reports;
(2) Performs in-depth quantitative and qualitative analysis and evaluations of material, and material handling in order to advise senior management of the effectiveness of the programs operations, to ensure management's goals and objectives are met and to make recommendations for process improvement;
(3) Performs data collection to measure productivity, improve quality, cut costs, and manage resources. (4) Collects and formats data for statistical analysis, and queuing analysis for all shop store material to provide upper management metrics that measure productivity and efficiency of services provided to NAVFAC customers;
(4) Researches industry best business practices to determine applicability and suitability of program improvement implementation;
(5) Develops executable plans to smoothly integrate changes with the least interruptions to day-to-day operations;
(6) Coordinates the positioning, allocation, reallocation, and replenishment of general consumable goods;
(7) Monitors consumption and reports indications of abuse to management for investigation;
(8) Analyzes historical cost data and material demands to project the expansion or reduction of on- the-shelf material, as well as the impact to the mission;
(9) Performs analysis and evaluations, both quantitative and qualitative, to improve the effectiveness of work methods and procedures, management controls, information systems and business practices;
(10) Provides input for command evaluations and strategic plans and must have working knowledge of MAXIMO principles and functionality, such as data input/output, and integrity of operational management. Must be able to interpret MAXIMO reports to track key elements of the Navy Working Capital Fund Expenditures.
Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

Details.Education:
In lieu of specialized experience, you may qualify with the following education or combination of both education and experience: For the NT-4: A Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree;
OR
Three full years of progressively higher level graduate education leading to a Ph.D. or equivalent degree;
OR
An LL.M. degree in a field directly related to the position being filled. OR For the NT-3: A Master's or equivalent graduate degree;
OR
Two full years of progressively higher level graduate education leading to a Master's or equivalent degree;
OR
An LL.B. or J.D. degree in a field directly related to the position being filled. A transcript must be submitted with your application if qualifying using education. See Required Documents for additional information.

MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
GS-12:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience equivalent to the next lower grade level GS-11 or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector performing the following duties: 1) Reviewing program risks and audit/assessment findings to determine management control effectiveness and recommending new management controls;
2) Presenting observations, findings and recommending changes to existing management practices;
3) Providing timely and quality customer support to charge card program participants and charge card program stakeholders and continually monitoring, assessing, and adjusting as appropriate, established charge card management controls;
4) Preparing training materials to ensure current charge card policy and program management requirements are accurately communicated and ensuring that all mandatory training requirements are met; 5) Conducting detailed analyses of complex functions and work processes and providing solutions to disputed issues. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

